04:14.020 --> 04:15.850
Buff-buff? Buboo-buboo?

04:16.260 --> 04:20.100
In any event, it looks like I'll have to 
work hard so I can fight on my own.

04:20.100 --> 04:21.390
I see.

04:21.390 --> 04:23.920
In that case, I know of 
an easy way to level up.

04:23.920 --> 04:24.860
Oh? What's that?

04:24.860 --> 04:29.730
I'll capture a monster and 
you can just keep attacking it!

04:29.730 --> 04:31.330
That's just being a bully!

04:31.720 --> 04:36.410
Even if it's to raise my level, continually 
hacking at an enemy that can't defend itself...

04:36.410 --> 04:38.520
That's something I just can't do.

04:38.520 --> 04:40.620
I thought it was a brilliant idea.

04:41.590 --> 04:44.190
Then, what about if you attack me?

04:44.190 --> 04:47.620
Since my level is so high, 
you should get tons of EXP, right?

04:47.620 --> 04:50.100
Me? Attack you, Maya-nee?

04:50.730 --> 04:52.890
That's something I can't do, either.

04:52.890 --> 04:55.560
The chances are very slim,
 but what if I hurt you?

04:56.650 --> 04:58.110
<b>Glomp</b>

04:56.650 --> 04:58.110
<b>Glomp</b>

04:56.670 --> 05:00.080
You're just the most <i>adorable </i>
little brother! I can't bear it!

05:00.080 --> 05:04.150
Can't you even just pause a little 
before attacking me like that?!

05:04.610 --> 05:09.680
Besides, leveling up slowly and distributing 
your upgrade points is the fun part.

05:09.680 --> 05:13.130
To get strong using a hack is 
to renounce all the fun of a game.

05:14.620 --> 05:16.090
What is it, Maya-nee?

05:16.090 --> 05:16.870
It's just...

05:16.870 --> 05:22.500
I always end every battle in one hit, so there's
 no point in you getting stronger, is there?

05:22.630 --> 05:22.670
<b>No Point</b>

05:22.670 --> 05:22.710
<b>No Point</b>

05:22.710 --> 05:23.880
<b>No Point</b>

05:24.970 --> 05:27.050
Y-You really didn't hold back.

05:27.050 --> 05:31.250
Besides, Asahi, if you stepped up 
and faced real danger, it'd be terrible!

05:31.250 --> 05:33.810
Even so, I want to get stronger!

05:33.810 --> 05:35.290
If I don't...

05:38.480 --> 05:38.650
<b>Hmmm</b>

05:38.480 --> 05:38.650
<b>Hmmm</b>

05:38.650 --> 05:38.730
<b>Hmmm</b>

05:38.650 --> 05:38.730
<b>Hmmm</b>

05:38.730 --> 05:39.400
<b>Hmmm</b>

05:38.730 --> 05:39.400
<b>Hmmm</b>

05:40.640 --> 05:44.780
For now, I'll leave any specialized training
 for when I've leveled up a bit more.

05:44.780 --> 05:47.090
And I'd like a new skill, so...

05:48.530 --> 05:49.990
<b>Glomp</b>

05:48.530 --> 05:49.990
<b>Glomp</b>

05:50.620 --> 05:54.410
You're done with your stats, right? 
Give your big sister some attention now.

05:54.960 --> 05:57.610
Stop pestering me all the time!

05:59.450 --> 06:01.040
<i>This skill... This is it!</i>

06:01.040 --> 06:03.420
Asahi!

06:06.590 --> 06:07.750
Asahi?

06:12.030 --> 06:14.260
A skill for slipping away: Escape.

06:14.260 --> 06:18.770
As long as I have this,
 I can escape Maya-nee's glomping!

06:15.520 --> 06:18.770
<b>Glomp</b>

06:15.520 --> 06:18.770
<b>Glomp</b>

06:19.230 --> 06:20.270
What?!

06:21.610 --> 06:25.030
<i>Got her. A rare taste of 
victory over Maya-nee!</i>

06:28.570 --> 06:30.860
Wh-What? What's wrong, Maya-nee?

06:31.560 --> 06:33.660
Didn't you know, Asahi?

06:33.880 --> 06:35.910
The more my prey tries to run away,

06:35.910 --> 06:38.660
the more fired up I get.

06:38.660 --> 06:41.190
Sh-She's a man-eater!

06:41.190 --> 06:41.920
But seriously...

06:42.180 --> 06:46.630
Don't make your little brother your prey!

06:44.110 --> 06:46.630
Asahi!

06:46.630 --> 06:48.100
Escape!

06:48.870 --> 06:49.470
Huh?

06:49.720 --> 06:53.220
I'm out of MP?! After just one use?!

06:57.310 --> 06:59.690
See? I caught you!

06:59.690 --> 07:02.100
You can't get away from your big sister!

06:59.690 --> 07:04.410
I should've put more points into my MP!

07:07.730 --> 07:12.030
If I keep relying on Maya-nee 
all the time, I'll never get stronger.

07:12.530 --> 07:17.040
Maybe I should try forming 
a party with someone else.

07:17.700 --> 07:22.790
<b>Lock-picking 
skills preferred!</b>

07:18.350 --> 07:20.810
All of these have really 
tough prerequisites.

07:18.500 --> 07:22.790
<b>Baggage carriers welcome!</b>

07:19.330 --> 07:22.790
<b>Need someone battle-ready</b>

07:20.250 --> 07:22.790
<b>10,000 mani a day</b>

07:20.790 --> 07:22.790
<b>Let's all get 
better 
together!</b>

07:20.810 --> 07:22.790
Are they looking for people for shady jobs?

07:21.250 --> 07:22.790
<b>We're a cozy 
clan that never 
stops smiling</b>

07:23.280 --> 07:28.140
<i>Still, I'd forgotten about it because 
I've been adventuring with Maya-nee,</i>

07:28.140 --> 07:32.050
<i>but joining a party is one of the 
real pleasures of isekai stories.</i>

07:32.730 --> 07:36.460
<i>Taking on a raid boss with everyone
 pooling their strengths for the battle,</i>

07:36.890 --> 07:42.060
<i>exploring lots of different places, eating 
and sleeping side-by-side, making memories...</i>

07:42.650 --> 07:46.610
<i>And maybe, just maybe, 
there'd be some romance, too?</i>

07:49.010 --> 07:51.050
Are you looking for party members?

07:51.050 --> 07:51.820
Oh, Tanya!

07:51.820 --> 07:54.720
This time of year, it's all 
people who didn't get picked.

07:54.720 --> 07:58.430
Like those, for example. 
They've been up for about two months.

07:59.570 --> 08:02.620
Can I ask? Have you been flying 
solo this whole time, Asahi-kun?

08:02.620 --> 08:05.210
No. I've been working with 
Maya—uh, my big sister.

08:05.210 --> 08:06.340
I see.

08:06.610 --> 08:10.940
So you must be the vanguard while your 
sister supports you from the rear, yeah?

08:10.940 --> 08:15.760
<i>Nope. Maya-nee annihilates everything, 
and I just watch from a distance.</i>

08:15.760 --> 08:20.060
You can put together a party however you like,
 but a famous one that's well-balanced...

08:20.060 --> 08:23.060
is the one Siegfried leads: Balmung!

08:24.460 --> 08:27.930
Gordon-san is a tank with
 impregnable defense.

08:27.930 --> 08:30.900
The sorceress, Mimosa-san,
 excels in every form of magic,

08:30.900 --> 08:33.210
and handles healing, buffs, and debuffs.

08:33.880 --> 08:37.140
The elven archer, Shuulain-san, 
is a long-range attacker,

08:37.740 --> 08:43.260
while Siegfried engages the enemy up close!

08:43.260 --> 08:46.110
It's the ideal party composition,
 don't you think?

08:46.110 --> 08:47.130
Wow.

08:47.130 --> 08:50.930
Splitting up roles in a party and 
fighting together sounds really great.

08:50.930 --> 08:54.260
Speaking of which, 
what's Siegfried-san doing now?

08:54.510 --> 08:57.100
He went to go defeat the 
Demon King, didn't he?

08:57.100 --> 09:00.640
Well, on the way, they nearly got 
wiped out by a mysterious enemy,

09:00.640 --> 09:03.180
so they fled and came back here.

09:03.180 --> 09:05.550
What? But they're Balmung!

09:05.550 --> 09:09.200
So true. What kind of fearsome 
enemy could have done it?

09:09.200 --> 09:10.880
Asahi-kun, you should be careful, too.

09:10.880 --> 09:12.030
Thanks.

09:12.030 --> 09:16.610
But seeing as you're the "hope of hopes," 
I'm sure you're being careful already.

09:17.940 --> 09:21.910
Well, for now, I guess I'll think on it 
a little more before joining a party.

09:25.050 --> 09:26.900
A party, huh?

09:26.900 --> 09:29.970
But if I team up with other 
people, Maya-nee will—

09:31.210 --> 09:32.380
Hey, wino!

09:32.380 --> 09:34.910
Why don't you watch where
 you're going, you dolt?

09:36.690 --> 09:39.300
Man, that hurt. My shoulder hurts like hell.

09:39.300 --> 09:42.680
You've dislocated my bro's shoulder!

09:42.680 --> 09:45.250
We're gonna need money to get him patched up!

09:42.680 --> 09:46.690
<i>Are they picking on a drunk? 
I'm staying out of it.</i>

09:46.690 --> 09:48.440
Gimme money for medical care!

09:48.440 --> 09:50.570
Yeah, give us your money!

09:50.570 --> 09:52.050
Money?

09:52.800 --> 09:55.610
I spent it all on alcohol.

09:55.610 --> 09:57.280
He's broke, bro.

09:57.510 --> 09:59.160
Tch. Forget this, then.

09:59.160 --> 10:01.290
He can just go ahead and die now.

10:05.450 --> 10:06.250
What the...

10:06.250 --> 10:09.120
Guess I couldn't just pretend 
I didn't see it after all.

10:09.120 --> 10:10.750
I'll keep them occupied.

10:10.750 --> 10:12.940
Use that time to escape!

10:13.300 --> 10:15.010
This little brat!

10:15.630 --> 10:18.760
<i>Okay! I'll draw them away, 
then use Escape to elude them!</i>

10:18.760 --> 10:19.510
Huh?

10:23.810 --> 10:25.930
What? Wh-Who <i>are</i> you?

10:31.370 --> 10:33.570
Th-That's impossible!

10:43.430 --> 10:46.070
<i>He took care of all three
 in less than a second.</i>

10:46.540 --> 10:48.880
<i>J-Just who is this guy?</i>

10:53.100 --> 10:55.090
<i>Seriously. Who is this guy?</i>

10:56.560 --> 10:57.750
Are you all right?

10:57.750 --> 11:00.460
Here, I'll rub your back for you.

11:00.460 --> 11:01.900
Thanks.

11:01.900 --> 11:03.470
Wait. You're...

11:04.040 --> 11:05.470
Aren't you...

11:06.250 --> 11:08.480
the guy from Balmung?

11:10.230 --> 11:12.220
Siegfried-san?

